  "query_preview": "..\n(This evening through next Sunday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: Smoke from regional wildfires will \ncontinue to impact visibility across portions of northern and \neast-central Nevada today, and may create respiratory issues for \nsome. \n\nStorm activity on Tuesday will be confined to mainly the UT border\nand extreme northeastern corner of Elko County. Monsoon moisture\nis slowly being shunted eastward as the HPC over the Panhandles\ncontinues to deepen and expand through the week. There exists a\nlow chance of storm activity over the UT border again Wednesday\nafternoon but beyond mid week the availability of moisture really\nbecomes cutoff as the HPC expands westward. A prolonged heat event\nis anticipated with probabilities of temperatures greater than\n100F climbing above 75% for local climate sites Friday through\nSunday. Long-term guidance keeps the HPC and hot, dry conditions\nover the region well into next week.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: High pressure builds in smoke \nboth today and through the week causing visibility and respiratory\nissues as area wildfire activity continues. High confidence \nexists in the warming trend expected later this week that will \nbring major HeatRisk to the region by Friday and the weekend.",
